    "Recipe1M+-style ingredient terms mapped onto the palette (snaq-parity Req 6.1, Decision 13).",
    "Matching: ingredient text is normalised (lowercase, punctuation stripped) and the LONGEST term appearing as a word-boundary phrase wins, so 'wholemeal bread' beats the generic 'bread' and 'chicken soup' is soup, not chicken.",
    "Targets are FOOD classes only — never background, unknown_food, or unsupported_liquid (Decision 20 food-channels-only).",
    "Deliberately no bare 'rice' term: it would capture rice vinegar / rice flour; unmapped ingredients are counted into the unmapped-ingredient rate instead."
